  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Fearless Foundation for the Arts</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Fearless Collective is led by young women artivists in Sri Lanka and India, using participatory public art and storytelling practices to reclaim space and strengthen feminist movements in the region and with grassroots community organizing in multiple countries around the world. Their team co-creates murals and facilitates workshops and community dialogue centering under-represented and mis-represented women and queer people, as well as developing digital multimedia content and platforms for movement-building. The grant will support the following specific priorities and activities; 1. Local art interventions, campaigns and films 2. Artist residencies 3. Staff salaries</narrative>
  </description>
